{"parentUuid":"c8bd58e3-abb7-4adb-af97-033e25ec376c","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5695120b75e50fb2","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01UgKoKuYqfsRrtEFaaJ74UN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JGhTLRjRbTVGFn5MaPLUc3","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"ULD scheduling logic-based Benders symmetric cut unit load device"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7219,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7219,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoy8kU5PmfvMRQagH6gX","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"ceddfbcc-d0b0-40b5-ae93-3b203906b092","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:37.730Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f43e5a2c-89f4-4c2c-a540-51f30a0937ed","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"a5695120b75e50fb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018k5zkLnKZKHmSy7mj7fTG8","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"symmetry-aware Benders cut decomposition orbit broadcasting\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A Framework for Handling and Exploiting Symmetry in Benders’ Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2511.22251\"},{\"title\":\"[2511.22251] A Framework for Handling and Exploiting Symmetry in Benders' Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.22251\"},{\"title\":\"A Framework for Handling and Exploiting Symmetry in Benders’ Decomposition – Optimization Online\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/2025/11/a-framework-for-handling-and-exploiting-symmetry-in-benders-decomposition/\"},{\"title\":\"A Framework for Handling and Exploiting Symmetry in Benders’ Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://www.arxiv.org/pdf/2511.22251v1\"},{\"title\":\"A Framework for Handling and Exploiting Symmetry in Benders’ Decomposition∗\",\"url\":\"https://www.arxiv.org/pdf/2511.22251\"},{\"title\":\"Benders decomposition - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benders_decomposition\"},{\"title\":\"Benders decomposition for the energy aware task scheduling of constellations of nanosatellites | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/378946927_Benders_decomposition_for_the_energy_aware_task_scheduling_of_constellations_of_nanosatellites\"},{\"title\":\"Benders decomposition - JuMP-dev\",\"url\":\"https://jump.dev/JuMP.jl/stable/tutorials/algorithms/benders_decomposition/\"},{\"title\":\"Benders Decomposition Approach for Generalized Maximal Covering and Partial Set Covering Location Problems\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2073-8994/17/9/1417\"},{\"title\":\"Benders decomposition for the energy aware task scheduling of constellations of nanosatellites | Computers and Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1016/j.cor.2024.106618\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about symmetry-aware Benders cut decomposition and orbit broadcasting:\n\n## Overview\n\nRecent work has developed a theory of symmetry detection within the Benders decomposition (BD) framework by introducing a tailored family of graphs that capture the symmetry information of both the Benders master problem and the Benders oracles.\n\n## Key Approaches\n\nThe research devises techniques for the separation and aggregation of symmetric Benders cuts by means of tailored separation routines and extended formulations, which substantially reduce the number of executions of the separation oracles.\n\nThe motivation for this work stems from the fact that automatic symmetry handling became a powerful component of modern MIP solvers, but BD cannot benefit from these techniques because MIP solvers are not aware of the symmetries of the cuts that are separated.\n\n## Practical Applications\n\nThe effect of both symmetry handling and cut aggregation has been shown for bin packing and scheduling problems. Symmetry handling only becomes effective when it is combined with exploiting symmetries in generating Benders cuts.\n\nThis framework represents an important advancement in making Benders decomposition more efficient by automatically detecting and leveraging the symmetries present in optimization problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"4dc1615d-10b6-44fe-a19f-db73691cdddb","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:43.170Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f43e5a2c-89f4-4c2c-a540-51f30a0937ed","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c8bd58e3-abb7-4adb-af97-033e25ec376c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"a5695120b75e50fb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S8sFsMDjCrtnQg7VpcnuV7","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CPAIOR 2025 symmetric Benders cut orbit isomorphic facilities\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A Framework for Handling and Exploiting Symmetry in Benders’ Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://www.arxiv.org/pdf/2511.22251v1\"},{\"title\":\"What’s Hot at CPAIOR (Extended Abstract) Claude-Guy Quimper Universit´e Laval\",\"url\":\"https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/AAAI/article/download/10640/10499\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR: Integration of AI and OR Techniques in Constraint Programming 2027 2026 2025 ...\",\"url\":\"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/program?id=574\"},{\"title\":\"A Framework for Handling and Exploiting Symmetry in Benders’ Decomposition∗\",\"url\":\"https://www.arxiv.org/pdf/2511.22251\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR 2025\",\"url\":\"https://sites.google.com/view/cpaior2025\"},{\"title\":\"[CPAIOR 2025] — Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/isaim/c/-zsNiQty_N8\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR 2025 : Integration of AI and OR Techniques in Constraint Programming\",\"url\":\"https://callforpaper.org/cfp/cpaior-2025-integration-of-ai-and-or-techniques-in-constraint-programming_227\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR 2025 : Integration of AI and OR Techniques in Constraint Programming\",\"url\":\"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/servlet/event.showcfp?copyownerid=90704&eventid=182533\"},{\"title\":\"AI4OPT Researchers Present Optimization Advances and Win Awards at CPAIOR 2025 | Artificial Intelligence Institute for Advances in Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.ai4opt.org/news-events/ai4opt-researchers-present-optimization-advances-and-win-awards-cpaior-2025\"},{\"title\":\"Benders Decomposition Approach for Generalized Maximal Covering and Partial Set Covering Location Problems\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2073-8994/17/9/1417\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about your query:\n\nA symmetric cut pool derived from a Benders cut (α, β) is defined as {(π⁻¹(α), β) : π ∈ Π}, where Π is a symmetry group. When Π is a symmetry group of a problem and (α, β) is a Benders cut, and if Π is isomorphic to a certain structure, a symmetric cut pool can be derived from that single Benders cut.\n\nThe research demonstrates key theoretical advances: if α⊤z+β ≤x is a Benders cut, then also π⁻¹(α)⊤z+β ≤x is a Benders cut, and a single Benders cut thus gives access to an entire family of symmetric Benders cuts.\n\nFor actions of the symmetric group, which arise in many applications, this family of symmetric cuts can be separated very efficiently, avoiding potentially expensive separation oracles, and an extended formulation can express an exponentially large family of Benders cuts by polynomially many inequalities.\n\nThe paper \"A Framework for Handling and Exploiting Symmetry in Benders' Decomposition\" appears in the search results from arXiv, which addresses exactly the topics in your query: handling symmetric Benders cuts in the context of orbit structures and isomorphic problems, relevant to facility location and similar optimization problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"f4a1d3fc-fd17-479f-8484-e8267ad5f615","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:43.853Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c8bd58e3-abb7-4adb-af97-033e25ec376c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ceddfbcc-d0b0-40b5-ae93-3b203906b092","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"a5695120b75e50fb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JGhTLRjRbTVGFn5MaPLUc3","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ULD scheduling logic-based Benders symmetric cut unit load device\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"ULD Build-Up Scheduling with Logic-Based Benders Decomposition | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-60597-0_17\"},{\"title\":\"OPUS 4 | ULD Build-Up Scheduling with Logic-Based Benders Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://opus4.kobv.de/opus4-zib/frontdoor/index/index/docId/9643\"},{\"title\":\"Planning and Scheduling by Logic-Based Benders Decomposition | Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/opre.1060.0371\"},{\"title\":\"Logic-based Benders decomposition for planning and scheduling: a computational analysis | The Knowledge Engineering Review | Cambridge Core\",\"url\":\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/knowledge-engineering-review/article/abs/logicbased-benders-decomposition-for-planning-and-scheduling-a-computational-analysis/70EE77BFAE516C56F3363A90A3786D84\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Planning and Scheduling by Logic-Based Benders Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220243896_Planning_and_Scheduling_by_Logic-Based_Benders_Decomposition\"},{\"title\":\"Computational Evaluation of Cut-Strengthening Techniques in Logic-Based Benders’ Decomposition | Operations Research Forum | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s43069-023-00242-3\"},{\"title\":\"Planning and Scheduling by Logic-Based Benders Decomposition J. N. Hooker\",\"url\":\"https://johnhooker.tepper.cmu.edu/planning2.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Stochastic Planning and Scheduling with Logic-Based ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2012.14074\"},{\"title\":\"Logic-based Benders decomposition with a partial assignment acceleration technique for avionics scheduling - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0305054822001769\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Logic-based Benders decomposition for planning and scheduling: a computational analysis\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/312096713_Logic-based_Benders_decomposition_for_planning_and_scheduling_a_computational_analysis\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant research on this topic. Here's what I discovered:\n\n## ULD Build-Up Scheduling with Logic-Based Benders Decomposition\n\nThe research addresses a complex planning and scheduling problem arising from the build-up process of air cargo pallets and containers, collectively referred to as unit load devices (ULD), in which ULDs must be assigned to workstations for loading.\n\n### The Problem Context\n\nSince air freight usually becomes available gradually along the planning horizon, ULD build-ups must be scheduled neither too early to avoid underutilizing ULD capacity, nor too late to avoid resource conflicts with other flights. Whenever possible, ULDs should be built up in batches, thereby giving ground handlers more freedom to rearrange cargo and utilize the ULD's capacity efficiently.\n\n### The Proposed Approach\n\nA logic-based Benders decomposition approach assigns batches to time intervals and workstations in the master problem, while the actual schedule is decided in a subproblem. By choosing appropriate intervals, the subproblem becomes a feasibility problem that decomposes over the workstations. Additionally, the similarity of many batches is exploited by a strengthening procedure for no-good cuts.\n\n### Performance Results\n\nThe approach solves 15% more instances to optimality and decreases run times by more than 50% in the geometric mean. This improvement is especially pronounced for longer planning horizons of up to one week, where the Benders approach solves over 50% instances more than the baseline.\n\nThis research was published in 2024 at the CPAIOR 2024 conference.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"7df40508-3ee7-479a-97d6-f74cffb0edfd","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:45.295Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ceddfbcc-d0b0-40b5-ae93-3b203906b092","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3b578b3d-5af2-4912-85f6-ec4c7300eaac","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"a5695120b75e50fb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PnZtRoxmns8zeLHYyefJq3","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"logic-based Benders decomposition symmetry breaking nogood cut LBBD\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Logic-Based Benders Decomposition - John Hooker\",\"url\":\"https://johnhooker.tepper.cmu.edu/encyLBBD.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Logic-Based Benders Decomposition: Theory and Applications | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-031-45039-6\"},{\"title\":\"Logic-Based Benders Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/logic-based-benders-decomposition-lbbd-4e47b3ae-690a-44a4-9d80-a191b385b4e6\"},{\"title\":\"Logic-Based Benders Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/386592005_Logic-Based_Benders_Decomposition\"},{\"title\":\"Combining optimisation and simulation using logic-based Benders decomposition - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S037722172300591X\"},{\"title\":\"Logic-Based Benders Decomposition for Large-Scale Optimization | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-22788-3_1\"},{\"title\":\"Stochastic Planning and Scheduling with Logic-Based Benders Decomposition | INFORMS Journal on Computing\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/ijoc.2022.1184\"},{\"title\":\"[1910.11944] Logic-based Benders decomposition for large-scale optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1910.11944\"},{\"title\":\"Computational Evaluation of Cut-Strengthening Techniques in Logic-Based Benders’ Decomposition | Operations Research Forum | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s43069-023-00242-3\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Logic-Based Benders Decomposition for Large-Scale Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/335669137_Logic-Based_Benders_Decomposition_for_Large-Scale_Optimization\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found about logic-based Benders decomposition, symmetry breaking, nogood cuts, and LBBD:\n\n## Overview\n\nLogic-based Benders decomposition (LBBD) is a substantial generalization of classical Benders decomposition that allows the subproblem to be any optimization problem rather than specifically a linear or nonlinear programming problem.\n\n## Nogood Cuts\n\nNogood (no-good) or exclusion cuts encode that the current master assignment leads to infeasibility in the subproblem. No-good cuts originate with the work of Balas and Jeroslow on unit hypercubes, where they are called canonical cuts and are the tightest inequalities which separate a single corner of the hypercube.\n\nNo-good inequalities are typically weak—causing slow convergence of the LBBD scheme. Consequently, cut-strengthening techniques that generate irreducible cuts outperform the greedy algorithm and the use of no cut strengthening.\n\n## Symmetry Breaking\n\nResearch has shown that symmetry-breaking constraints are used in MILP models aimed at minimizing makespan. Computational results demonstrate the effectiveness of proposed symmetry-breaking constraints and various types of cuts.\n\n## Inference Duality\n\nLBBD derives a cut from the inference dual of the subproblem, which is the problem of finding the tightest bound on the optimal value that can be logically deduced from the constraints.\n\nThe search results provide a comprehensive foundation for understanding how LBBD combines these concepts to improve optimization problem solving.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"dee14508-cb1d-406c-bd8a-05554643a532","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:47.063Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3b578b3d-5af2-4912-85f6-ec4c7300eaac","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
