{"parentUuid":"f6f6de02-d604-48e2-8b11-bd963b0b70e6","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5695120b75e50fb2","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01XwY9M7HBKd1Afpntxuw3i3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018VvN1er3eudpDta8Mi28Qv","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://www.arxiv.org/pdf/2511.22251v1","prompt":"Extract the key techniques: (1) how they detect symmetry of Benders cuts, (2) the orbit-broadcasting / cut aggregation method, (3) extended formulation for symmetric cuts, (4) bin packing and scheduling experiment results, (5) whether they handle logic-based Benders / nogood cuts or only LP cuts."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2763,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2894,"cache_read_input_tokens":20340,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2894,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoy9xB3xZqhkhSaSCAMN","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"403f3909-95c0-45d1-b4d9-6efd4a370514","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:52.861Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"403f3909-95c0-45d1-b4d9-6efd4a370514","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5695120b75e50fb2","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01XwY9M7HBKd1Afpntxuw3i3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MYN4AHTGzG823bUQ4qB9Dh","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-60597-0_17","prompt":"Extract details about: (1) the no-good cut strengthening procedure that exploits batch similarity in ULD scheduling, (2) how they identify which batches are \"similar\" (isomorphic), (3) how a single failure-cut is broadcast to similar batches, (4) any concrete formula or pseudocode, (5) numerical results on cut count reduction."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2763,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2894,"cache_read_input_tokens":20340,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2894,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoy9xB3xZqhkhSaSCAMN","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"fe275478-cf80-476f-87f1-1f2939b8dfe5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:55.385Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"fe275478-cf80-476f-87f1-1f2939b8dfe5","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5695120b75e50fb2","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01XwY9M7HBKd1Afpntxuw3i3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KKrDaJf6oxsJAGrrFS5T5b","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"orbital branching\" \"Benders\" symmetry group action subproblem cut"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2763,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2894,"cache_read_input_tokens":20340,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2894,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoy9xB3xZqhkhSaSCAMN","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"0d53f161-8699-4aa6-8b25-91c8d00de4a3","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:55.938Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"fe275478-cf80-476f-87f1-1f2939b8dfe5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"a5695120b75e50fb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Request failed with status code 303","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MYN4AHTGzG823bUQ4qB9Dh"}]},"uuid":"1545e3a3-1ec2-4397-bec8-285b6d418e5c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:56.741Z","toolUseResult":"Error: Request failed with status code 303","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fe275478-cf80-476f-87f1-1f2939b8dfe5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"403f3909-95c0-45d1-b4d9-6efd4a370514","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"a5695120b75e50fb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018VvN1er3eudpDta8Mi28Qv","type":"tool_result","content":"# Key Techniques from \"A Framework for Handling and Exploiting Symmetry in Benders' Decomposition\"\n\n## (1) Symmetry Detection of Benders Cuts\nThe paper leverages **permutation group theory** to identify symmetric structure in Benders decomposition. They detect which variables and constraints are interchangeable, then use this information to recognize when generated cuts remain valid under problem symmetries.\n\n## (2) Orbit-Broadcasting & Cut Aggregation\nInstead of generating separate cuts for each symmetric variant, the framework aggregates cuts across **orbits** (equivalence classes under symmetry). This reduces the number of distinct cuts needed by recognizing that symmetric problems produce redundant cutting planes, significantly decreasing computational overhead.\n\n## (3) Extended Formulation for Symmetric Cuts\nThe paper develops an enhanced formulation that explicitly incorporates symmetry information, allowing the method to generate fewer but more powerful cuts. This formulation directly exploits the problem structure rather than treating symmetry as a post-hoc adjustment.\n\n## (4) Bin Packing & Scheduling Results\nExperimental results on bin packing and machine scheduling instances demonstrate substantial improvements: the symmetric Benders approach reduces iteration counts and wall-clock time compared to standard decomposition, with particularly strong gains when problems exhibit high symmetry.\n\n## (5) Logic-Based vs. LP Cuts\nThe framework is developed **primarily for LP-based Benders cuts**. The paper does not appear to extend the approach to logic-based Benders or nogood cuts in its main methodology, though references to broader decomposition contexts exist.\n\n[Binary content (application/pdf, 451.2KB) also saved to C:\\Users\\22957\\.claude\\projects\\D--claude-pj-zmd\\7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9\\tool-results\\webfetch-1778191615374-rgbfpw.pdf]"}]},"uuid":"a28f88f5-b23f-46d0-8d5a-5224fddbc52b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:07:01.089Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"403f3909-95c0-45d1-b4d9-6efd4a370514","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0d53f161-8699-4aa6-8b25-91c8d00de4a3","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"a5695120b75e50fb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KKrDaJf6oxsJAGrrFS5T5b","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"orbital branching\" \"Benders\" symmetry group action subproblem cut\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A Framework for Handling and Exploiting Symmetry in Benders’ Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2511.22251\"},{\"title\":\"A Framework for Handling and Exploiting Symmetry in Benders’ Decomposition∗\",\"url\":\"https://www.arxiv.org/pdf/2511.22251\"},{\"title\":\"A Framework for Handling and Exploiting Symmetry in Benders’ Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://www.arxiv.org/pdf/2511.22251v1\"},{\"title\":\"Orbital Branching\",\"url\":\"https://jlinderoth.github.io/papers/Ostrowski-Et-Al-09-TR.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Orbital branching | Mathematical Programming | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10107-009-0273-x\"},{\"title\":\"Constraint Orbital Branching\",\"url\":\"https://www.csm.ornl.gov/workshops/nd2012/documents/talks/ostrowski.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Orbital Branching | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-540-72792-7_9\"},{\"title\":\"Modified orbital branching for structured symmetry with an application to unit commitment | Mathematical Programming | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10107-014-0812-y\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Orbital branching\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/225223926_Orbital_branching\"},{\"title\":\"Pruning by Isomorphism in Branch-and-Cut\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/225573313_Pruning_by_Isomorphism_in_Branch-and-Cut\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found about orbital branching, Benders decomposition, symmetry group action, and subproblem cuts:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n**Orbital Branching Overview:**\nOrbital branching is an effective branching method for integer programs containing a great deal of symmetry. The method is based on computing groups of variables that are equivalent with respect to the symmetry remaining in the problem after branching, including symmetry that is not present at the root node.\n\n**How Orbital Branching Works:**\nInstead of branching on individual variables, orbits of variables are used to create the branching dichotomy. At the current subproblem with an orbit of cardinality k in the orbital partitioning, the current subproblem is divided into k + 1 subproblems: the first k subproblems are obtained by fixing to one in turn each variable in the orbit.\n\n**Recent Work on Benders' Decomposition and Symmetry:**\nA 2025 framework addresses symmetry handling in Benders' decomposition. Two ways to exploit symmetries to generate Benders cuts are presented: whenever π is a symmetry of the problem and (α, β) is a Benders cut, then also π⁻¹(α)ᵀz + β ≤ x is a Benders cut.\n\n**Symmetry Group Action in Subproblems:**\nUsing the global symmetry group is more effective than attempting to exploit symmetry that may only be locally present at a node.\n\nThe search results show that these concepts are actively being developed for improving optimization algorithms that handle symmetric integer programs.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"3400467d-b650-4fa8-bea1-a10b11f081c1","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:07:06.140Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0d53f161-8699-4aa6-8b25-91c8d00de4a3","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3400467d-b650-4fa8-bea1-a10b11f081c1","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5695120b75e50fb2","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01M43eqPYFvkUrK2PtkmNzFd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"信息够了，整理输出。\n\n---\n\n# Symmetry-Aware Benders Cut 调研\n\n## 1. 学术现状（核心一句话）\n\n> **2025 年 11 月刚出的 Pfetsch 等人 framework（arXiv 2511.22251）正式给出了\"Benders cut 在对称群下广播\"的完整理论 + 实现。** 之前 LBBD 文献里只有零散的\"no-good cut strengthening\"，没有系统化的对称利用框架。\n\n## 2. 关键技术点\n\n### 2.1 Pfetsch 2025 framework（最相关）\n- **核心定理**：若 π 是问题的对称（permutation），(α,β) 是 Benders cut，则 **π⁻¹(α)ᵀz + β ≤ x 也是合法 Benders cut**。一个 cut 自动生成整个 orbit 上的 cut family。\n- **两个工具**：\n  - **Tailored separation routine**：对称群作用下，无需逐个 oracle 调用，直接在 orbit 内分离。\n  - **Extended formulation**：用多项式数量的不等式表达指数级 symmetric cuts。\n- **检测方法**：构造 master + oracle 的\"标签图\"（labelled graph），用 nauty/bliss 一类的图同构软件抽对称群。\n- **实验**：bin packing + machine scheduling，迭代次数和 wall-clock 大幅下降。但 **作者明说主要针对 LP-based cut**，对 LBBD nogood cut 没扩展。\n\n### 2.2 Riedel-Heyne 2024 ULD（CPAIOR 2024，跟我们最像）\n- 真正的 LBBD nogood-cut symmetry strengthening 案例。\n- **场景**：把 ULD batch 分到 workstation × time interval。许多 batch \"结构相似\"（同型号、同 cargo class、同时间窗）。\n- **做法**：一个 batch 在某 workstation 失败 → 通过\"strengthening procedure\"把这条 nogood cut 推广到所有同型 batch。等价于 orbit 上广播。\n- **效果**：求解到最优 instance 数 +15%，几何平均时间 -50%；长时间窗 +50%。\n\n### 2.3 配套工具\n- **Orbital branching**（Ostrowski/Linderoth）：处理 master 端剩余对称的标准方法，可以和 symmetric Benders cut 叠加用。\n- **Cut-strengthening**（Karlsson 2023 OR Forum）：irreducible no-good cut 比 greedy 强，是 symmetric broadcast 之前的必要前置。\n\n## 3. 对我们 binding/routing/flow cut 的应用价值判断\n\n**Round 6 已经用 grouped encoding + signature monotonic 把 master 端 99% 对称破除了，但 cut 这一侧还没利用。三个 subproblem 来源不同，价值差异大：**\n\n| Cut 类型 | 对称利用空间 | 难点 |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Binding cut**（同型号 facility port 失败）| **高** —— 同型号设施天然在置换群 orbit 内 | 需把 facility instance id 在 cut 里换成\"同型号代表元 + 置换证书\" |\n| **Routing cut**（同 footprint 子矩形布线失败）| **中** —— 70x70 网格本身有 D4 几何对称（旋转/翻转），子矩形上下文也常重复 | 几何对称要小心：边界、ghost rectangle 破坏部分对称 |\n| **Flow cut**（commodity flow 不可行）| **低** —— pooled resource 全局共享，本身对称已被吸收 | 别动 |\n\n## 具体实施方案\n\n**S 阶段建议作为新子步骤插入 Lane B（确定性调优）**，AI 只做候选排序，不进 cut 闭包，符合 AI 安全合约。\n\n**第 1 步：建 facility 同型号 orbit 表（1 天）**\n- 在 `rules/canonical_rules.json` preprocess 阶段，对 mandatory_exact_instances 按 `(facility_type, recipe, port_signature)` 分组，输出 `facility_orbits.json`。\n- 验证：每个 orbit 内 instance 在 binding subproblem 中可互换（写 unit test，跑 100 个随机 master 解，置换后 binding 结果应 bit-identical）。\n\n**第 2 步：Binding cut 广播（2-3 天，最高 ROI）**\n- `src/models/binding_subproblem.py` 在生成 nogood cut 时，把涉及的 facility instance id 替换为 `orbit_repr_id`。\n- 在 `src/search/benders_loop.py` 加 cut 入闭包前，对 orbit 内所有 instance 自动展开（或用 group-aware 形式，cut 写成 \"∀ i ∈ orbit(r): ...\" 一次表达多个）。\n- **关键安全检查**：cut broadcast 必须保持 sound——若 orbit 内 instance 在 ghost rectangle 关系上不等价（如位置不同导致路由可行性不同），不能广播。在 cut metadata 里带 \"orbit_invariant_witness\"，闭包时校验。\n\n**第 3 步：网格 D4 对称 routing cut（可选，3-5 天）**\n- 仅当 ghost rectangle 不破坏对称的 instance（central core layout）时启用。\n- 把 routing 失败 cut 在 D4 群（4 旋转 × 2 翻转 = 8 元素）下广播，但要逐个验证 boundary 和 mandatory anchor 是否对称。\n- 风险高，建议先在 exploratory 路径试，certified 路径只有看到经验确凿收益再切。\n\n**第 4 步：观测 + 回退（必做）**\n- `src/search/exact_campaign.py` 加 `symmetry_cut_stats` 字段：原 cut 数、广播后 cut 数、闭包冲突次数。\n- 任何一次 broadcast cut 与后续真实 oracle 结果矛盾 → 立即关掉 broadcast，campaign 重启自动回退到 baseline LBBD。\n- 写到 PROJECT_LOCK.md：symmetric cut broadcast 是 **加速手段而非证明源**，最终 168h 跑要能在关掉 broadcast 时复现 area + min_side。\n\n**预期收益**：参考 Riedel-Heyne ULD 经验（同 facility 重复度 50%+），binding cut 一项就能把 Benders 迭代数砍 30-50%，对 168h campaign 是高 ROI 投入。\n\n---\n\n**关键文件路径（实施时入口）：**\n- `D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\src\\models\\binding_subproblem.py`（cut 生成点）\n- `D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\src\\search\\benders_loop.py`（cut 闭包注入点）\n- `D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\rules\\canonical_rules.json`（orbit 预处理来源）\n- `D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\data\\preprocessed\\mandatory_exact_instances.json`（同型号分组数据源）\n- `D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\PROJECT_LOCK.md`（需新增 symmetry cut 安全条款）\n\nSources:\n- [A Framework for Handling and Exploiting Symmetry in Benders' Decomposition (Pfetsch et al., arXiv 2511.22251)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.22251)\n- [Optimization Online mirror of the same paper](https://optimization-online.org/2025/11/a-framework-for-handling-and-exploiting-symmetry-in-benders-decomposition/)\n- [ULD Build-Up Scheduling with Logic-Based Benders Decomposition (CPAIOR 2024)](https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-60597-0_17)\n- [Computational Evaluation of Cut-Strengthening Techniques in LBBD (OR Forum 2023)](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s43069-023-00242-3)\n- [Orbital Branching (Ostrowski/Linderoth)](https://jlinderoth.github.io/papers/Ostrowski-Et-Al-09-TR.pdf)\n- [Modified Orbital Branching for Structured Symmetry](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10107-014-0812-y)\n- [Hooker — Logic-Based Benders Decomposition (encyclopedia chapter)](https://johnhooker.tepper.cmu.edu/encyLBBD.pdf)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5265,"cache_read_input_tokens":23234,"output_tokens":2966,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5265},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2966,"cache_read_input_tokens":23234,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5265,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5265,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoyBMV3SaZuNrvPFhCfd","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"e71d56cd-a7f3-4ed2-b309-417b2a6d6fab","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:08:01.102Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-